req.body is the parsed JSON body (Requirement 7.2), and parsed maps keep the
body's key order (Requirement 3.5).

### echo keeps key order and nesting
POST /echo

{"zeta": 1, "alpha": {"b": [1, 2.5, "three", null, true], "a": {}}, "mid": "x"}
=> 200

{"zeta": 1, "alpha": {"b": [1, 2.5, "three", null, true], "a": {}}, "mid": "x"}

### fields of the body
POST /summon

{"name": "Vlad", "tags": ["count", "vampire"], "age": 593, "alive": false}
=> 200

{"name": "Vlad", "firstTag": "count", "tagCount": 2, "nextAge": 594, "undead": true}

### an array body
POST /echo

[1, "two", {"three": 3}]
=> 200

[1, "two", {"three": 3}]
